WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.680
Series, RNA and Cellular Memory, Season 1, Episode 1.

00:05.680 --> 00:09.400
Ever wondered how our cells remember their function throughout their lifetime?

00:09.400 --> 00:13.600
The answer lies in the fascinating world of RNA and cellular memory.

00:13.600 --> 00:19.360
RNA, or ribonucleic acid, is a pivotal molecule that orchestrates the complex symphony of

00:19.360 --> 00:20.360
our genes.

00:20.360 --> 00:25.460
It's the maestro, meticulously conducting the coding-decoding regulation and expression

00:25.460 --> 00:26.460
of our genes.

00:26.460 --> 00:28.280
Now, let's delve a little deeper.

00:28.280 --> 00:34.800
RNA exists in two main forms, messenger RNA, commonly known as mRNA, and non-coding RNA,

00:34.800 --> 00:36.480
or NCRNA.

00:36.480 --> 00:39.760
Each has its unique part to play in this grand performance.

00:39.760 --> 00:44.480
The mRNA is the diligent courier, transmitting genetic instructions from DNA to the machinery

00:44.480 --> 00:46.560
that synthesizes proteins.

00:46.560 --> 00:51.360
On the other hand, NCRNA, while not directly involved in protein synthesis, holds crucial

00:51.360 --> 00:55.320
regulatory roles, influencing various biological processes.

00:55.360 --> 01:00.360
In this intricate dance of life, RNA in its diverse forms is the unsung hero, silently

01:00.360 --> 01:04.040
shaping the workings of our cells and ensuring they remember their roles.

01:04.040 --> 01:09.040
RNA, in its diverse forms, is the unsung hero of cellular function and memory.

01:09.040 --> 01:11.360
Now, dive into the cellular realm.

01:11.360 --> 01:15.680
Here every cell has a memory, a blueprint of its function and behavior.

01:15.680 --> 01:20.320
This is the phenomenon of cellular memory, a concept that has intrigued scientists for

01:20.320 --> 01:21.320
years.

01:21.320 --> 01:25.560
The cell in our body has a unique role, whether it's a muscle cell contracting or a neuron

01:25.560 --> 01:27.040
transmitting signals.

01:27.040 --> 01:29.800
But how do cells remember these roles?

01:29.800 --> 01:32.920
Enter RNA, the unsung hero of cellular memory.

01:32.920 --> 01:38.040
RNA, or ribonucleic acid, serves as a messenger, carrying the instructions from DNA to the

01:38.040 --> 01:39.520
rest of the cell.

01:39.520 --> 01:44.840
It ensures that even as cells divide and multiply, they retain their unique identities.

01:44.840 --> 01:49.440
This is crucial for maintaining the specialized functions of different types of cells.

01:49.560 --> 01:54.760
RNA essentially acts as a cellular memoir, preserving a record of a cell's identity

01:54.760 --> 01:55.760
and function.

01:55.760 --> 01:59.880
So, the next time you marvel at the complexity of life, remember this.

01:59.880 --> 02:05.580
Just like humans, every cell carries with it a memory of its past, a legacy of its function.

02:05.580 --> 02:11.000
With the basics in place, it's time to connect the dots between RNA and cellular memory.

02:11.000 --> 02:16.760
Now, RNA, in all its diverse forms, plays a pivotal role in dictating cellular memory.

02:16.760 --> 02:21.440
Through both coding and non-coding types, RNA helps each cell remember its designated

02:21.440 --> 02:24.400
role, maintaining the harmony within our bodies.

02:24.400 --> 02:25.400
Consider this.

02:25.400 --> 02:29.740
Our skin cells, brain cells, liver cells, all have the same DNA, yet they all perform

02:29.740 --> 02:30.800
distinct roles.

02:30.800 --> 02:32.320
How is that possible?

02:32.320 --> 02:34.060
It's the rRNA, my friend.

02:34.060 --> 02:39.480
It reads the DNA's blueprint and helps each cell understand and remember its unique function.

02:39.480 --> 02:42.680
This complex interaction is not just a biological marvel.

02:42.680 --> 02:47.680
It's the key to our survival, our health, and our understanding of diseases.

02:47.680 --> 02:52.560
When this interaction goes awry, it can lead to a myriad of health issues, from cancer

02:52.560 --> 02:54.640
to neurodegenerative disorders.

02:54.640 --> 03:00.880
RNA and cellular memory, two complex concepts, intertwine to drive the beautiful symphony

03:00.880 --> 03:01.600
of life.

